{"unit_slug":"paladin_lay_on_hands","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"hp_pool","justification":"Lay On Hands tracks a continuous HP budget (not discrete uses) that is partially expendable per activation. The current use_count atom implies discrete tokens; here the resource is a pool of HP points that scales as 5 × paladin level and can be drawn in any amount per activation (1 HP to remaining max). Multiple activations can draw from the same pool until exhausted. This is fundamentally different from use_count and cannot be expressed with any existing UseCountCap variant.","evidence":"You have a pool of healing power that replenishes when you finish a Long Rest. With that pool, you can restore a total number of Hit Points equal to five times your Paladin level."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"remove_condition","justification":"A new ClassFeatureEffect variant is needed to represent removing a condition from a target creature. This is distinct from apply_condition (which exists in mastery effects) and from heal_hp. The Poisoned removal costs 5 HP from the pool but does NOT restore HP — so it is not a heal variant either.","evidence":"You can also expend 5 Hit Points from the pool of healing power to remove the Poisoned condition from the creature; those points don't also restore Hit Points to the creature."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"branched_effect_choice","justification":"The unit offers two distinct activation modes (heal HP, or remove Poisoned for 5 HP) as an either/or player choice within a single Bonus Action use. ClassFeatureActivationMechanics carries a single effect field; there is no branched-choice shape to represent this. A new variant or a multi-effect composition shape is needed.","evidence":"As a Bonus Action, you can touch a creature and draw power from the pool ... You can also expend 5 Hit Points from the pool of healing power to remove the Poisoned condition."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'bonus_action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'heal' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_numeric_bonus' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.83}
worker.sh: done paladin_lay_on_hands (source=srd-5.2.1, claude_exit=0)
{"unit_slug":"rogue_sneak_attack","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"class_feature_passive_on_hit_rider","justification":"Sneak Attack is a passive conditional on-hit damage rider that fires automatically when attack conditions are met, not an explicit activation. The `ClassFeatureActivationMechanics` family requires player-initiated activation and a rest-based use-count reset. A new payload family composing on_hit_window + damage + use_count/turn_start_window + conditional gate is needed.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack roll if you have Advantage on the roll and the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"per_turn (RestResetCadence)","justification":"Sneak Attack's use-count resets at the start of each turn, not on a short or long rest. `RestResetCadence` only supports rest-based resets (short_or_long_rest, long_rest, short_rest, partial_short_full_long). A turn-based reset variant connecting use_count to turn_start_window is required.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage..."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"conditional_prerequisite_gate (advantage_or_ally_adjacency)","justification":"The feature fires only when: (a) the rogue has Advantage on the attack roll, OR (b) an ally is within 5 feet of the target AND that ally is not Incapacitated AND the rogue does not have Disadvantage. This compound condition check has no atom in v4 taxonomy. The `requires` relation exists but there is no predicate atom for advantage state or ally positioning.","evidence":"if you have Advantage on the roll... You don't need Advantage on the attack roll if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the target, the ally doesn't have the Incapacitated condition, and you don't have Disadvantage on the attack roll."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"weapon_passthrough (DamageType)","justification":"The extra damage has the same type as the weapon's damage type. DamageType is a closed 13-value enum (acid, bludgeoning, cold, ...). There is no 'weapon' or 'same_as_weapon' passthrough variant. Encoding it as any fixed type would be incorrect.","evidence":"The extra damage's type is the same as the weapon's type."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"weapon_property_filter (finesse_or_ranged)","justification":"The on-hit trigger only applies when the attack uses a weapon with the Finesse or Ranged property. No weapon property filter exists for class feature mechanics (or for on_hit_window in general). The mastery trigger has 'weapon_hit' and 'weapon_hit_melee_only' but no Finesse/Ranged variant.","evidence":"the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'heal' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_die_count' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":2.053}
